# Host-side published ports (all bind to 127.0.0.1). The commented values are
# the defaults. `make up` (tools/ports) writes an alternative here when a
# default is taken; set one yourself to force a port (`make env-init` creates
# .env from this file). Docker Compose, the Makefile, and tools/ports all
# read .env, so keep it to plain KEY=number lines: no quotes, no
# ${VAR:-default}, no empty values. Delete or comment a line to use the default.
#POSTGRES_PORT=5432
#PRICING_PORT=8000
#GRPC_PORT=50051
#SHIPMENT_MGMT_PORT=8080
#RELAY_MGMT_PORT=8081
#CONSUMER_MGMT_PORT=8082
#KAFKA_HOST_PORT=19092
#KAFKA_UI_PORT=8085
#PROMETHEUS_PORT=9090

# Failure-scenario knob: delay every pricing quote (ms). 0 = normal.
#PRICING_ARTIFICIAL_DELAY_MS=0
